B.cg9=new A.pO("Micropreemie","Micro-LBW","<750 g","Birthweight below 750 g \u2014 extreme end of the extremely-low birth weight spectrum.","Highest risk of mortality, IVH, NEC, BPD, ROP, and long-term neurodevelopmental impairment. Requires tertiary NICU care with surfactant, early CPAP/mechanical ventilation, and parenteral nutrition from Day 1.",B.mj,null,749)
B.cgd=new A.pO("Extremely Low Birth Weight","ELBW","<1000 g","Birthweight below 1000 g regardless of gestational age.","Very high risk of respiratory distress syndrome, IVH, NEC, sepsis, and PDA. Surfactant, early TPN, antenatal steroids, and strict fluid/glucose management required. Long-term neurodevelopmental follow-up mandatory.",B.ad,null,999)
B.cga=new A.pO("Very Low Birth Weight","VLBW","1000\u20131499 g","Birthweight 1000 g or more but less than 1500 g.","High risk of RDS, PDA, and IVH. Most require NICU admission for respiratory support, early nutrition, and glucose/thermal regulation. Better short-term survival than ELBW but similar risk categories.",B.aG,1000,1499)
B.cge=new A.pO("Low Birth Weight","LBW","1500\u20132499 g","Birthweight 1500 g or more but less than 2500 g.","Elevated risk of hypothermia, hypoglycaemia, feeding difficulties, and neonatal sepsis. Many can be managed in SCBU/SNCU with kangaroo mother care (KMC). Lower long-term morbidity than VLBW but still requires close observation.",B.fK,1500,2499)
B.cgb=new A.pO("Normal Birth Weight","NBW","2500\u20133999 g","Birthweight 2500 g or more but less than 4000 g.","Routine newborn care. Rooming-in with mother, early breastfeeding, standard screening (blood sugar, bilirubin, SpO\u2082, hearing). Low baseline risk of perinatal complications.",B.ab,2500,3999)
B.cgc=new A.pO("Macrosomia (High Birth Weight)","HBW","\u22654000 g","Birthweight 4000 g or more. Grade II \u22654500 g; Grade III \u22655000 g.","Increased risk of shoulder dystocia, birth injury (brachial plexus, clavicle fracture), hypoglycaemia (especially in infant of diabetic mother), polycythaemia, and NICU admission. Screen for maternal diabetes; monitor blood glucose in first 24\u201348 h.",B.cz,4000,null)
